  "notes": "Drawn from one clear 2026 left-side photo of a 737-8 (levelled for the climb); the fin's fine halftone dots and several thin stripes are simplified to three white stripes and one mid-blue sweep. The belly is white except the aft tail. Right side not checked: the wordmark is the same there. Re-checked 2026-11-15 on A6-FKF: 'fly' and 'dubai' are one wordmark in two colors, now one title with parts, x 0.151 to 0.442 on dubai's baseline (lowercase 0.7 of the ascenders); the i's orange dot isn't carried. Heights left as drawn (the photo is a climbing view, rotated 12°). The aft fuselage's arc and stripes and the fin's sweeps are curves: smooth (the fin's root fillet stays straight).",
  "history": "Replaced Skyarium v1's approximation. flydubai's scheme since launch (2009), refined when the 737 MAX arrived; unchanged in essentials."
}
